{"format":1,"key":"zone:dunmorogh","path":"/lore/zone/dunmorogh","name":"Dun Morogh","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"dunmorogh","name":"Dun Morogh","path":"/lore/zone/dunmorogh"},"levels":"Levels 1-10","description":"Dun Morogh is a snow-swept mountain highland situated at the heart of Khaz Modan. It serves as the ancestral starting ground and shared homeland for the…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:dunmorogh","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Dun Morogh is a snow-swept mountain highland situated at the heart of Khaz Modan. It serves as the ancestral starting ground and shared homeland for the dwarves of Ironforge and the displaced gnomes of Gnomeregan. Though guarded by towering peaks and fortified passes, the snowy realm faces rising internal threats from troggs, Frostmane trolls, and irradiated leper gnomes.","Dun Morogh occupies the highest peaks in the Eastern Kingdoms, an alpine expanse ringed by jagged summits that shield it from Searing Gorge to the south and the Wetlands to the north. These snowy mountains feed the rivers flowing across Khaz Modan and provide near-limitless veins of copper and iron. Access is heavily restricted to mountain tunnels like North Gate Pass and South Gate Pass, watched closely by dwarven Mountaineers. At the heart of the region sits Ironforge, an ancient subterranean wonder and the capital of King Magni Bronzebeard's realm, linked straight to Stormwind by the marvel of the Deeprun Tram."],"hash":"ee26fa","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"dfc37e7ef9","sec":61},"female-narrator":{"sha":"68003c07b9","sec":63}}},{"id":"zone:dunmorogh#faq1","part":"faq","anchor":"faq1","title":"What races start in Dun Morogh?","paras":["What races start in Dun Morogh?","Both dwarves and gnomes begin their journeys here in Coldridge Valley, a sheltered basin in southwestern Dun Morogh, before venturing out through Coldridge Pass into Kharanos and the wider zone."],"hash":"ef89a7","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"77534c0963","sec":14},"female-narrator":{"sha":"af4b0ef4b8","sec":16}}},{"id":"zone:dunmorogh#faq2","part":"faq","anchor":"faq2","title":"What happened to Gnomeregan?","paras":["What happened to Gnomeregan?","During the Third War, a subterranean race called troggs swarmed Gnomeregan. In an attempt to purge the invaders, High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque released radioactive gas into the lower levels. The plan failed catastrophically, killing thousands and irradiating many gnomes into crazed leper gnomes, forcing the healthy survivors to flee to Ironforge."],"hash":"a69ecb","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"144abd9126","sec":24},"female-narrator":{"sha":"e58e2164e0","sec":25}}},{"id":"zone:dunmorogh#faq3","part":"faq","anchor":"faq3","title":"How do you leave Dun Morogh on foot?","paras":["How do you leave Dun Morogh on foot?","Dun Morogh is walled in by high mountain ridges. To travel eastward into Loch Modan on foot, take the roads leading to North Gate Pass or South Gate Pass in the northeastern mountains. You can also travel directly to Stormwind City via the Deeprun Tram inside Ironforge."],"hash":"681af6","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"3ad2853cfe","sec":20},"female-narrator":{"sha":"2bc2f9ce84","sec":21}}},{"id":"zone:dunmorogh#faq4","part":"faq","anchor":"faq4","title":"Where is the flight master in Dun Morogh?","paras":["Where is the flight master in Dun Morogh?","The only functional Alliance flight master in the zone is located inside the Great Forge of Ironforge, connecting travelers to locations across Khaz Modan, Stormwind, and the northern Alliance outposts."],"hash":"4e1b9a","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"af9f8221dd","sec":16},"female-narrator":{"sha":"f72672a7ce","sec":16}}},{"id":"zone:dunmorogh#faq5","part":"faq","anchor":"faq5","title":"Who are the Frostmane trolls?","paras":["Who are the Frostmane trolls?","The Frostmane are a tribe of ice trolls who ruled Dun Morogh long before the dwarves emerged from Uldaman. Though defeated and driven into the crags generations ago, they remain bitter enemies of Ironforge, routinely raiding dwarven farms and roads from retreats like Frostmane Hold."],"hash":"bd9caa","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"cdca3acada","sec":20},"female-narrator":{"sha":"a5891c0da8","sec":21}}},{"id":"zone:dunmorogh#faq6","part":"faq","anchor":"faq6","title":"What is Kharanos?","paras":["What is Kharanos?","Kharanos is the primary dwarven settlement in central Dun Morogh. It houses the Thunderbrew Distillery, trainers, and supplies, serving as the central operational hub for young adventurers and Mountaineers tackling local troll and wildlife problems."],"hash":"78a443","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"2729086c70","sec":17},"female-narrator":{"sha":"d03d4bcff3","sec":17}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Dun Morogh (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dun_Morogh_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Dun Morogh","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dun_Morogh"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/zone/ironforge","n":"Ironforge","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/gnomeregan","n":"Gnomeregan","k":"dungeon"},{"p":"/lore/zone/lochmodan","n":"Loch Modan","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/kharanos","n":"Kharanos","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/coldridge-valley","n":"Coldridge Valley","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/deeprun-tram","n":"Deeprun Tram","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/gol-bolar-quarry","n":"Gol'Bolar Quarry","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/anvilmar","n":"Anvilmar","k":"subzone"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/amberstill-ranch","n":"Amberstill Ranch","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/anvilmar","n":"Anvilmar","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/brewnall-village","n":"Brewnall Village","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/chill-breeze-valley","n":"Chill Breeze Valley","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/coldridge-pass","n":"Coldridge Pass","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/coldridge-valley","n":"Coldridge Valley","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/frostmane-hold","n":"Frostmane H